ts\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p><strong>For years, the nation’s capital was allowed to decay — marred by crime, graffiti, and crumbling infrastructure — amid a bureaucratic acceptance of decline as inevitable.</strong> President Donald J. Trump rejected that surrender from Day One — and under his leadership, the Trump Administration is demonstrating that decline is a choice.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>This week, the historic cascading fountain at Meridian Hill Park <a href=\"https://wjla.com/news/local/historic-washington-dc-fountain-flows-again-after-years-meridian-hill-park-malcolm-x-national-park-service-department-interior-trump-250th-birthday\">roared</a> <a href=\"https://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2026/may/16/fountain-flows-dcs-meridian-hill-park-idling-7-years/\">back</a> <a href=\"https://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2026/may/16/fountain-flows-dcs-meridian-hill-park-idling-7-years/\">to</a> <a href=\"https://x.com/AdamsMorganNews/status/2055327574302101610\">life</a> after years of <a href=\"https://dcist.com/story/18/09/13/why-dont-the-fountains-at-meridian/\">disrepair</a>. What was once a stark symbol of <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/wheres-the-water-in-the-nations-capital-dry-fountains-mar-the-landscape/2017/07/09/29f5282a-6342-11e7-a4f7-af34fc1d9d39_story.html\">all-too-common neglect</a> now flows powerfully again as a visible emblem of rebirth in the heart of the city.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1880\" height=\"1253\" src=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/meridian-hill-park-comp-2.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-42061\" style=\"width:700px\" srcset=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/meridian-hill-park-comp-2.jpg 1880w, https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/meridian-hill-park-comp-2.jpg?resize=600,400 600w, https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/meridian-hill-park-comp-2.jpg?resize=768,512 768w, https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/meridian-hill-park-comp-2.jpg?resize=1200,800 1200w, https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/meridian-hill-park-comp-2.jpg?resize=1536,1024 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1880px) 100vw, 1880px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>This is about far more than water and landscaping; it’s about rekindling national pride in the city that represents the American Republic.</strong> These projects signal a fundamental shift: a rejection of mediocrity and a renewed commitment to excellence in the place where our democracy is on display. It’s a signal to the world — and every citizen — that we will not settle for inferiority in the city that embodies our republic.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>President Trump promised to Make America Great Again — and that includes making our capital beautiful, safe, and worthy of the greatest nation on Earth. Where past Administrations offered excuses and stagnation, the Trump Administration is delivering real results. Dozens of additional restoration, infrastructure, and beautification <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/03/making-the-district-of-columbia-safe-and-beautiful/\">projects</a> are now underway across Washington, D.C., as the nation prepares to celebrate its 250th anniversary on July 4, 2026.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Decline is a choice. President Trump is choosing action, beauty, strength, and pride.</strong></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/05/decline-is-a-choice-president-trump-restores-pride-and-beauty-to-americas-capital/\">Decline Is a Choice: President Trump Restores Pride and Beauty to America’s Capital</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
